<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George II of Abkhazia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George II was king of Abkhazia in the first half of the 10th century, when the kingdom, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutaisi">Kutaisi</a>, was the leading power of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. He extended its rule into Kartli in the east and was a patron of Georgian-language church life. Later kings such as Constantine III continued this expansion before the throne passed to the Bagratid Bagrat III in 978.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-ii-of-abkhazia.jpg" alt="George II of Abkhazia" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alaexis · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_II_fassade_stone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
